unding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 against main is open with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed: 2.665 should round to 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit (08d3cd5986).\n- **PR:** The request to open the PR timed out, but the PR had actually been created, so I didn't retry and risk a duplicate. It was missing alex as a reviewer, so I added him separately.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory lookup didn't recognise it. The fix follows the description in the code and the test. I haven't merged the PR, since that needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PHEKeJpGPT3U8bipFqjL1L", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XnerFe1Bgz8qCLbZ1sYfhq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01EyjsLk263ocSjoodzgbPYi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QLopbSKBxWeFp1NwnG5MHZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Sb83o7rfPmLhkhE8VTnbej", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "conte